WEBVTT

00:00:03.180 --> 00:00:11.980
Intrigue in the Bakumatsu

00:00:26.200 --> 00:00:29.840
Tsukikage kooru daichi wo

00:00:29.840 --> 00:00:33.670
Korogari fumiwakete yuku

00:00:33.670 --> 00:00:40.880
Horobi to saisei no jidai ga hajimaru

00:00:40.880 --> 00:00:44.550
Jiyuu wo omoku kakagete

00:00:44.550 --> 00:00:48.120
Michinaki michi wo erande

00:00:48.120 --> 00:00:55.230
Mahiru yori mabushii nichibotsu wo koete

00:00:55.230 --> 00:01:02.230
Yume wo kataru you ni toki no fune wa yuku

00:01:02.230 --> 00:01:11.340
Sono yamiji no mukou ni atarashii yoake

00:01:12.110 --> 00:01:19.250
Bokura wa kitto kurayami no kaina kara umarete kita

00:01:19.250 --> 00:01:22.790
Kanawanu koi wo suruyou ni

00:01:22.790 --> 00:01:26.760
Hikari e to samayotteku

00:01:26.760 --> 00:01:32.000
Doko made mo hateshino nai kono michi wo

00:01:32.000 --> 00:01:37.490
Kaeru sube wa nai

00:02:47.140 --> 00:02:48.300
Where is he?

00:03:27.010 --> 00:03:32.580
Right now I'm free, embraced by her
tenderness! I'm completely free!

00:03:33.820 --> 00:03:35.790
To protect her...

00:03:36.150 --> 00:03:37.850
Yojiro Akizuki...

00:03:38.360 --> 00:03:39.690
I'll kill you!

00:03:52.140 --> 00:03:53.000
You're not going to get away!

00:04:13.990 --> 00:04:15.320
There's no way out.

00:04:16.360 --> 00:04:19.230
Yeah... But I'll put an end to this!

00:04:30.210 --> 00:04:32.230
Those annoying flies...

00:05:46.020 --> 00:05:47.280
Shit!

00:05:47.550 --> 00:05:49.650
We've lost two ships...

00:05:49.920 --> 00:05:53.650
No one told me the
Republic Army was this powerful!

00:06:09.640 --> 00:06:10.610
What?

00:06:10.880 --> 00:06:12.870
The sky is bleeding!

00:06:13.080 --> 00:06:14.170
How ominous...

00:06:17.020 --> 00:06:18.680
Blood has been shed!

00:06:18.880 --> 00:06:20.680
Shed for victory!

00:06:21.390 --> 00:06:24.580
Don't stop moving forward, my comrades!

00:06:25.220 --> 00:06:29.060
Don't stop moving forward, my comrades!

00:06:29.590 --> 00:06:33.530
Show them the power of the Republic!

00:06:42.370 --> 00:06:43.360
Leader...

00:06:44.080 --> 00:06:48.670
Together with him! Together with our Republic!

00:06:52.380 --> 00:07:08.100
Together with the Republic!
Together with the Republic!

00:07:10.770 --> 00:07:12.530
Jeanne d'Arc, huh?

00:07:13.240 --> 00:07:16.500
So she invoked our French hero, huh?

00:07:17.280 --> 00:07:19.380
But it's just a play.

00:07:19.380 --> 00:07:24.540
Now I truly understand that we should never let
some random author write history!

00:07:25.320 --> 00:07:26.910
<i>"THE MYSTERIOUS TALE</i>
<i>OF THE GHOST-SEALING</i>
<i>MOON TEAR ASSASSIN"</i>
<i>ROLE: KAKUNOJO YUYAMA</i>

00:07:27.790 --> 00:07:32.690
They're completely different from French
civilians who defeated a corrupt monarchy.

00:07:33.320 --> 00:07:38.130
Tell me how a pack of dogs like that
is going to build a beautiful nation!

00:07:40.230 --> 00:07:45.330
There was a man who said
something very similar before.

00:07:45.700 --> 00:07:46.600
Oh?

00:07:47.170 --> 00:07:50.140
He was neither writer nor audience member.

00:07:51.010 --> 00:07:55.110
He destroyed the stage he chose
to perform on and then fled,

00:07:55.110 --> 00:07:57.510
saying he'd perform on a bigger stage...

00:07:58.050 --> 00:07:59.810
Ryoma Sakamoto, huh?

00:08:01.890 --> 00:08:04.550
So you made this play because of him?

00:08:05.220 --> 00:08:06.660
Don't give me that nonsense!

00:08:06.660 --> 00:08:08.890
Look at this castle! Look at Enomoto!

00:08:09.190 --> 00:08:14.960
I don't know what kind of witchcraft you used,
but either way this is no revolution!

00:08:15.500 --> 00:08:17.130
This is no nation!

00:08:18.540 --> 00:08:25.810
The request submitted by Jules Brunet and his
subordinates to return to their unit is granted.

00:08:25.810 --> 00:08:29.970
They return home via Yokohama and Saigon.

00:08:30.380 --> 00:08:51.900
For the Republic! With the Republic!
For the Republic! With the Republic!

00:09:28.110 --> 00:09:32.310
Tayu, it's not safe around here.
Maybe we should...

00:09:32.310 --> 00:09:36.280
I wonder what's going to happen... Seriously...

00:09:36.280 --> 00:09:42.710
Exactly! Now that it's come to this
I think we should get together and...

00:09:47.790 --> 00:09:50.780
You must be Lady Kotoha.

00:09:51.100 --> 00:09:53.590
Has Katsu-sensei been doing well?

00:09:53.870 --> 00:10:03.170
I'm sorry, but I'm associated with someone
close to him, but not directly with him.

00:10:03.170 --> 00:10:06.630
But this will get to him, won't it?

00:10:07.580 --> 00:10:12.310
I'll take that for you. Do you have
any message for him?

00:10:12.950 --> 00:10:17.480
I hate to admit it, but maybe
he was right all along...

00:10:18.020 --> 00:10:23.390
That man... He's no good... He's dangerous.

00:10:24.430 --> 00:10:30.800
I've already decided that I'm going to watch
until the curtain falls.

00:10:30.970 --> 00:10:33.490
I'll be sure to tell him that.

00:10:36.170 --> 00:10:41.210
Hey, Tayu, it's a problem. She's a spy, right?

00:10:41.210 --> 00:10:43.540
Moreover, she's connected to Kaishu Katsu...

00:10:44.080 --> 00:10:47.750
But at this rate things will
be much worse for this place.

00:10:48.890 --> 00:10:52.290
I really appreciate your concern,

00:10:52.290 --> 00:10:56.460
but if you're planning to go back to Yokohama,
find someone else to do it with.

00:10:56.460 --> 00:10:57.830
What? Hey!

00:10:57.830 --> 00:10:59.990
Don't be so cold, Tayu!

00:11:00.300 --> 00:11:01.000
But this isn't enough to make me give up on you!

00:11:01.000 --> 00:11:04.430
It looks like he's got quite the vixen
working for him, huh?
But this isn't enough to make me give up on you!

00:11:05.000 --> 00:11:07.100
Katsu Awanokami Kaishu...

00:11:07.670 --> 00:11:10.310
It's inevitable that sooner or later
he'll eventually work out a far-sighted scheme

00:11:10.310 --> 00:11:12.880
and make inroads with the New Government,

00:11:12.880 --> 00:11:15.310
which means he'll become an enemy someday.

00:11:16.380 --> 00:11:18.280
But I've already taken measures.

00:11:20.690 --> 00:11:22.850
I hope you have no objection.

00:11:24.760 --> 00:11:27.520
Well, just wait and see the result.

00:11:50.110 --> 00:11:54.280
Who are you? Let me guess.
Is this what you're after?

00:11:54.890 --> 00:11:58.820
This is something a beautiful
woman tearfully wrote.

00:11:59.260 --> 00:12:02.160
And it is now in the hands of
another beautiful woman.

00:12:02.690 --> 00:12:04.250
You'll have to kill me to get it!

00:12:11.740 --> 00:12:16.370
I'm freezing! Hey, why don't we stop
and get something to drink?

00:12:16.740 --> 00:12:18.370
I guess we could.

00:12:19.240 --> 00:12:20.470
Now you're talking!

00:12:21.310 --> 00:12:25.210
Hey, Mister! Can we get some sake?

00:12:29.590 --> 00:12:30.550
Who are you?

00:12:30.890 --> 00:12:31.860
You sneaking vixen!

00:12:34.630 --> 00:12:35.420
Die!

00:12:37.400 --> 00:12:38.860
T-Tayu!

00:12:39.130 --> 00:12:40.030
How dare you?!

00:12:50.910 --> 00:12:52.030
You're that guy from back then!

00:12:52.640 --> 00:12:54.040
So that means Enomoto is...

00:12:54.410 --> 00:12:56.210
Sensei, too?

00:12:57.420 --> 00:12:59.010
Tayu, are you okay?

00:12:59.250 --> 00:13:04.210
I'm not going to die...
The curtain hasn't fallen yet...

00:13:04.720 --> 00:13:08.060
I haven't seen the end of it... I can't die...

00:13:08.260 --> 00:13:11.300
A kabuki actor and a prostitute!

00:13:11.300 --> 00:13:12.390
Shut up!

00:13:13.000 --> 00:13:15.500
We're both better than you two samurai!

00:13:15.500 --> 00:13:16.730
What did you say?

00:13:19.670 --> 00:13:22.900
You! You're no ordinary playboy.

00:13:23.640 --> 00:13:25.510
So what?

00:13:35.650 --> 00:13:37.020
We need a doctor!

00:13:37.020 --> 00:13:37.920
You got it!

00:13:41.760 --> 00:13:43.090
I won't forgive him!

00:13:43.360 --> 00:13:46.760
Even if it's the Master, I still won't forgive him!

00:13:49.000 --> 00:13:53.630
He has... He has his own agenda...

00:13:55.310 --> 00:14:01.870
So forgive him...
Please take care of him for me...

00:14:04.220 --> 00:14:06.340
Tayu!

00:14:16.990 --> 00:14:18.790
Shiryokaku

00:14:23.900 --> 00:14:28.870
On this day, after the fall of Shiryokaku, the fortress
that had been bolstering the Republic's rear,

00:14:28.870 --> 00:14:34.040
the anti-Republic Yuguntai and
a group of civilians rally together.

00:14:34.480 --> 00:14:39.650
They collaborate with the New Government Army's
forces and begin their march,

00:14:39.650 --> 00:14:41.310
seizing strategic points all across the area.

00:14:41.890 --> 00:14:48.310
After sacrificing many lives, they finally begin
to close in on Goryokaku, however...

00:15:05.340 --> 00:15:06.670
What's happening?

00:15:20.460 --> 00:15:31.170
We've brought what you desire.

00:15:31.170 --> 00:15:36.040
Long time no see, young one.

00:15:36.610 --> 00:15:45.450
After the demise of Shinsaku Takasugi,
the founder of the legendary Kiheitai,

00:15:45.450 --> 00:15:49.120
the Head vanished; you have
once again found it...

00:15:49.120 --> 00:15:57.080
Once, we were defeated and forced
to leave the stage of history.

00:15:57.530 --> 00:16:02.430
Thanks to you, that which we have
greatly desired for five hundred years...

00:16:02.970 --> 00:16:09.340
All of this is to purge the poison
from this rotten nation...

00:16:09.340 --> 00:16:14.300
and create a beautiful, cherished nation.

00:16:18.820 --> 00:16:20.370
Now is the time.

00:16:39.770 --> 00:16:42.270
Why are you hesitating?

00:16:42.270 --> 00:16:45.500
The enemy is right in front of us! Charge!

00:16:55.420 --> 00:16:57.680
What the... Is this some kind of magic?

00:18:04.290 --> 00:18:05.160
Kamikaze!

00:18:05.160 --> 00:18:07.420
The gods are on the Republic's side?

00:18:46.600 --> 00:18:54.060
Once, many young orphans
gathered in our village of Koma.

00:18:55.040 --> 00:18:56.470
The reason for this was...

00:18:56.470 --> 00:19:00.180
...find the wielder of the Yin Moontear Sword.

00:19:00.180 --> 00:19:06.550
In other words, to find the one with the destiny
to be the new Eternal Assassin.

00:19:06.850 --> 00:19:11.820
The sword chose a child, and that was...

00:19:11.820 --> 00:19:14.660
Yojiro.

00:19:15.690 --> 00:19:22.330
The rest were sent out for adoption;
no one knew what became of them after that.

00:19:24.100 --> 00:19:33.480
Who knew the wielder of the Yang Moontear
was among those children?

00:19:42.550 --> 00:19:45.890
It is now clear who my enemy is.

00:19:46.620 --> 00:19:51.360
I shall risk my life and attack her
with the Yin Moontear.

00:19:51.730 --> 00:19:56.500
Now is the time for me to fulfill my destiny
as the Eternal Assassin.

00:20:03.270 --> 00:20:10.040
If I ever see her again, I promise
I'll kill her in one stroke with my sword.

00:20:10.550 --> 00:20:11.420
This means...

00:20:11.420 --> 00:20:17.480
If that's his desire, let us accept it
no matter how it is to end.

00:20:18.060 --> 00:20:23.990
It is our duty as the ones who sent him
out as the Eternal Assassin.

00:21:58.580 --> 00:22:02.380
<i>GORYOKAKU</i>
<i>EMERGES</i>

00:22:03.560 --> 00:22:09.330
Sono te wa ai no tsurugi

00:22:09.330 --> 00:22:18.370
Subete no hajimari no akashi

00:22:19.140 --> 00:22:25.100
Hikaru sora no hate

00:22:25.550 --> 00:22:30.320
Yume wa mada maboroshi

00:22:31.460 --> 00:22:34.560
Tsuki no akari kage ouyouni hashiru kono michi

00:22:34.560 --> 00:22:42.070
Tsuki no akari kage ouyouni hashiru kono michi

00:22:42.070 --> 00:22:47.840
Chigireta ai no tsurugi

00:22:47.840 --> 00:23:00.080
Sashidasu saki wa ikusen no namida ga hitotsu ni nari

00:23:00.080 --> 00:23:05.890
Ashita wo kagayakaseru

00:23:05.890 --> 00:23:11.600
Kono te wa ai no tsurugi

00:23:11.600 --> 00:23:20.300
Subete no hajimari no akashi

00:23:32.720 --> 00:23:47.430
EPISODE 26
TO GO
TOWARDS
THE SEA

00:23:34.380 --> 00:23:36.550
Yojiro Akizuki...

00:23:36.550 --> 00:23:41.860
Just like I thought, you managed to break
my bloody destiny of 500 years.

00:23:42.090 --> 00:23:44.500
Everything was just a dream...

00:23:45.100 --> 00:23:47.430
Now the curtain of the play written
by Sotetsu Ibaragi is falling.

00:23:47.430 --> 00:24:02.540
TO GO
TOWARDS
THE SEA

00:23:47.430 --> 00:23:50.400
Now the curtain of the play written
by Sotetsu Ibaragi is falling.

00:23:50.400 --> 00:23:51.970
Sensei!

00:23:52.140 --> 00:23:57.270
Ryoma, the world, which exists beyond
this sea that you wanted to see...

00:23:57.570 --> 00:24:00.910
I'll go out there and see it with my own eyes!
